  "query_preview": "..Much like those old-school ditto-machines I grew-\nup with...churning out identical, damp and very aromatic purple\nworksheets, today weather will be a nearly identical carbon-copy\nof yesterday. The upper pattern is defined by an anomalously\nstrong upper-low parked over central California this morning\nwith a decreasing gradient of southwest winds extending from \nwest to east across Southeast Arizona. Observed breezy surface \nwinds yesterday stayed in-check, remaining between 15 and 25 mph\nwith occasional gusts to 35 mph (west of Tucson). The upper-low\nitself isn't going to move much today besides another vort-lobe\nrotating along the western periphery into the base of the mean \ntrough. With this in mind, we can expect similar below normal \ntemperatures and winds to yesterday. The big difference will be \nsky cover, with thickening high clouds expanding across the \nforecast area today. Although winds will likely remain breezy \ntoday, we will still see elevated to near critical fire weather \nconditions again today. \n\nThe upper-low begins to eject NE into the Great basin Friday,\nthen the N through the northern Rockies this weekend. The\nsoutherly periphery of the trough axis will swing thru our neck\nof the woods Friday, increasing winds a tick Friday over today's\nreadings, especially areas east of Tucson. This will continue \nthe elevated fire weather conditions another day (Friday), \nbefore relaxing this weekend.\n\nThere is a slight change to the evolution of the upper pattern\nthan we have been advertising the past few days. With a strong \nand amplified ridge extending from the Southern Plains up into \nupper Midwest, we see the upper-ridge build farther east into \nthe central states. This position will still allow for moisture\nto push into the eastern portions of the forecast area the \nmiddle of next week, but it may be more limited than if the\nupper high was centered over the Four Corners region. At this\ntime, it looks like there will be enough moisture to result in\nisolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms mainly east of \nTucson. However, confidence is low at this time.",
